description:
Implement the Verilog module based on the following description.
Given the combinational logic circuit described below.

// Build this circuit in Verilog.

// Input b goes to two different two-input gates: a NAND and a NOR gate. Each of the two gates is connected to the input of a D flip-flop and then the flip-flop outputs go to a two-input OR, whose output is Z. The second input of the NAND is its corresponding flip-flop's output, and the second input of the NOR is its corresponding flip-flop's complemented output.
module comb_module2 (
	input clk,
	input b,
	output z);

code:
module comb_module2 (
	input clk,
	input b,
	output z);reg [1:0] state = 0;

	always @(posedge clk) begin
		state <= { ~(state[1] & b), ~(state[0] | ~b) };
	end

	assign z = state[1] | state[0];

endmodule

