Design a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary input (hex) into a corresponding 7-segment display output (symbol) for hexadecimal digits. The conversion occurs on each positive clock edge, where specific combinations of the binary input will activate specific segments of the display, representing the hexadecimal digits from 0 to F. In cases where the input does not correspond to a valid hexadecimal digit, the output will default to a specific segment configuration.
