Create a Verilog module that implements the following description. Assume signals are positive clock/clk edge triggered unless otherwise stated. Assume that the D flip-flops are initially reset to zero before the machine begins.

// Construct a circuit as follows:
// Input x goes to a three-input AND gate, a three-input OR gate, and a three-input NOR gate. The outputs of these gates go to D flip-flops. The outputs of the D flip-flops are connected to a three-input NAND gate, whose output is T.
module fsm_module1 (
	input clk,
	input x,
	output t);

code:
module fsm_module1 (
	input clk,
	input x,
	output t);reg [2:0] state = 0;

always @(posedge clk) begin
	state <= { state[2] & x & state[1], state[1] | x | state[0], ~(state[0] | x | state[2]) };
end

assign t = ~(state[2] & state[1] & state[0]);

endmodule

